IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Victoria): the rules about time, in one self-contained module.
-- It imports only the two libraries that ship with l4, so that it can be copied unchanged, by itself, into other work.
-- Its tests are in vic-tests-time.l4.
--
-- What it answers, each from the section named in the function's own name:
--   when an Act, a provision or a subordinate instrument comes into operation (the day, and the moment within the day);
--   how a period expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a day is counted, and which day is its last;
--   what happens when that last day is a holiday;
--   what "month", "year", "midnight", "financial year" and "calendar year" mean;
--   when service by post is taken to be effected;
--   the dates that the Act itself names.
-- Where the text does not answer, a function returns NOTHING (not covered), and a test asserts it.
-- Public holidays are never built in: the caller supplies the list for the place where the act is to be done (s 44(4)(b)).
-- Nothing is taken from how any court counts time.

§ `Types`

-- How a period of time is expressed in relation to a day (s 44(1) and (2)).
-- The first two begin the period at the day, the next two end it at the day.
-- "after" and "before" are not mentioned by s 44(1) or (2).
DECLARE VicPeriodEdge IS ONE OF
    VicBeginsOnDay
    VicReckonedFromDay
    VicEndsOnDay
    VicReckonedToDay
    VicAfterDay
    VicBeforeDay

-- The units a period can be expressed in. The text defines month and year (s 44(6)); it does not define day or week.
DECLARE VicPeriodUnit IS ONE OF
    VicDays
    VicWeeks
    VicCalendarMonths
    VicYears

-- A point of time within a day, as the Act words it.
DECLARE VicMomentWithinDay IS ONE OF
    VicBeginningOfDay      -- "at the beginning of that day" (ss 11(1), 11(2A), 24)
    VicLastMomentOfDay     -- "until the last moment of that day" (ss 12, 25)
    VicEndOfDay            -- "the point of time at which that day ends" (s 44(6)(a), midnight)

DECLARE VicMoment HAS
    `the day`              IS A DATE
    `the point within it`  IS A VicMomentWithinDay

-- What s 11 says about an Act or provision whose day is fixed by a proclamation.
DECLARE VicCommencement IS ONE OF
    VicNotYetInOperation
    VicInOperationFrom HAS `the moment` IS A VicMoment

DECLARE VicPostMethod IS ONE OF
    VicOrdinaryPost
    VicRegisteredPostOrCertifiedMail

§ `Part I -- the dates the Act names`

-- src:28 | 2 Commencement
-- src:29 | This Act shall come into operation on 1 July 1984.
@ref s 2 (src:28-29)
`s2 day the Act came into operation` MEANS Date 1 7 1984

-- src:73 | (e) in the case of an Act passed before 1 January 1986, the number of that Act only; and
@ref s 9(2)(e) (src:73)
`s9(2)(e) last day of the period in which an Act is cited by its number only` MEANS Date 31 12 1985

-- src:74 | (f) in the case of an Act passed on or after 1 January 1986, the calendar year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year.
@ref s 9(2)(f) (src:74)
`s9(2)(f) first day of the period in which an Act is cited by year and number` MEANS Date 1 1 1986

-- src:95 | (3) If an Act passed on or after 1 September 1985 does not authorize its citation by a short title, the long title of the Bill for the Act does not form part of the Act.
@ref s 10(3) (src:95)
`s10(3) first day on which an Act passed without a short title leaves its long title out of the Act` MEANS Date 1 9 1985

-- src:238 | (1) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in an Imperial Act or an Act of the Governor and Legislative Council of the colony of New South Wales in force in Victoria on 1 July 1851—
-- src:239 | (a) to the colony or the colony of New South Wales or the territory of New South Wales or the district of Port Phillip shall be construed as a reference to Victoria;
-- src:240 | (b) to the Governor of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to the Governor of Victoria;
-- src:241 | (c) to the Colonial Secretary of the colony of New South Wales or the Superintendent of Port Phillip shall be construed as a reference to the responsible Minister of the Crown in Victoria for the time being administering the provision in which the reference occurs;
-- src:242 | (d) to the Supreme Court of the colony of New South Wales or any judge of that Court or to any other court in that colony or to any judge, justice or other person presiding in any such court shall be construed as a reference to the court, judge or other person having a similar jurisdiction in Victoria;
-- src:243 | (e) to a justice of the peace in and for the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to a justice of the peace in and for Victoria;
-- src:244 | (f) to any officer or other person in the public service of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to an officer or other person having similar duties in the public service of Victoria; and
-- src:245 | (g) to the Government Gazette of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to the Victoria Government Gazette.
@ref s 21(1) (src:238-245)
`s21(1) day on which Imperial and New South Wales Acts are read as references to Victoria` MEANS Date 1 7 1851

-- src:246 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any Act (by whatsoever Parliament passed) in force in Victoria on 21 November 1856 to the Legislative Council shall be construed as a reference to the Legislative Council of Victoria and the Legislative Assembly of Victoria.
@ref s 21(2) (src:246)
`s21(2) day on which an Act is read as referring to the Legislative Council of Victoria` MEANS Date 21 11 1856

-- src:495 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
@ref s 36(1A)(a) (src:495)
`s36 first day of the period in which headings, examples, notes, diagrams and punctuation form part of an Act` MEANS Date 1 1 2001

-- src:758 | (2) In an Act or subordinate instrument, a reference to Standards Australia includes a reference to the Standards Association of Australia as constituted before 1 July 1999.
@ref s 38AA(2) (src:758)
`s38AA(2) day Standards Australia took over from the Standards Association of Australia` MEANS Date 1 7 1999

-- src:823 | (a) an Act that is passed, or a subordinate instrument that is made, on or after 1 July 2015; or
@ref s 38EA(2)(a) (src:823)
`s38EA(2) first day on which registered medical practitioner is defined` MEANS Date 1 7 2015

-- src:1124 | (a) whose name was, at any time within the three months immediately before 26 January 1984, enrolled on—
-- src:1125 | (i) an electoral roll for an electoral district of the Legislative Assembly; or
-- src:1126 | (ii) an electoral roll maintained under any one of the Commonwealth Acts known as the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918, the Australian Capital Territory Representation (House of Representatives) Act 1973 and the Northern Territory Representation Act 1922; or—
@ref s 55(2)(a) (src:1124-1126)
`s55(2)(a) day before which the three months are counted` MEANS Date 26 1 1984

-- src:1264 | purported appointment means a purported appointment of a non-citizen to a public office that was made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before section 64A came into operation.
@ref s 64B(1) "purported appointment" (src:1264)
`s64B(1) first day of the period of a purported appointment` MEANS Date 3 3 1986

-- The text does not state the day s 64A came into operation. Endnote 2 (Table of Amendments), which is not part of the Act (s 36(3)),
-- gives "ss 57, 58, 60, 61 on 10.12.25" for Act No. 55/2025, and the margin notes of ss 64A and 64B say they were inserted by section 61 of that Act.
-- src:1675 | | Commencement Date: | S. 59 on 13.11.25: s. 2(2); ss 57, 58, 60, 61 on 10.12.25: s. 2(1) |
@ref endnote 2 commencement of ss 57, 58, 60 and 61 of Act No. 55/2025 (src:1675)
`endnote 2 day sections 57, 58, 60 and 61 of Act No. 55/2025 came into operation` MEANS Date 10 12 2025

-- s 64B(1): the period ends immediately before s 64A came into operation, so its last day is the day before that day.
-- src:1264 | purported appointment means a purported appointment of a non-citizen to a public office that was made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before section 64A came into operation.
@ref s 64B(1) "purported appointment" (end of the period) (src:1264)
GIVEN dayS64ACameIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s64B(1) last day of the period of a purported appointment` MEANS dayS64ACameIntoOperation MINUS 1

-- s 64B(1): a purported appointment is one made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before s 64A came into operation.
-- src:1264 | purported appointment means a purported appointment of a non-citizen to a public office that was made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before section 64A came into operation.
@ref s 64B(1) "purported appointment" (the appointment was made in the period) (src:1264)
GIVEN dayTheAppointmentWasMade IS A DATE, dayS64ACameIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` MEANS
    dayTheAppointmentWasMade AT LEAST `s64B(1) first day of the period of a purported appointment` AND dayTheAppointmentWasMade LESS THAN dayS64ACameIntoOperation

§ `Part II -- s 44: periods of time`

-- src:1005 | (1) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a particular day, that day shall not be included in the period.
-- src:1006 | (2) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to end on, or to be reckoned to, a particular day, that day shall be included in the period.
@ref s 44(1) and s 44(2) (src:1005-1006)
GIVEN edge IS A VicPeriodEdge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER edge
    WHEN VicBeginsOnDay THEN JUST FALSE        -- s 44(1): "that day shall not be included"
    WHEN VicReckonedFromDay THEN JUST FALSE    -- s 44(1)
    WHEN VicEndsOnDay THEN JUST TRUE           -- s 44(2): "that day shall be included"
    WHEN VicReckonedToDay THEN JUST TRUE       -- s 44(2)
    WHEN VicAfterDay THEN NOTHING              -- the text is silent on a period "after" a day
    WHEN VicBeforeDay THEN NOTHING             -- the text is silent on a period "before" a day

-- src:1005 | (1) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a particular day, that day shall not be included in the period.
@ref s 44(1) (src:1005)
GIVEN edge IS A VicPeriodEdge, anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(1) first day counted in a period expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER edge
    WHEN VicBeginsOnDay THEN JUST (anchor PLUS 1)
    WHEN VicReckonedFromDay THEN JUST (anchor PLUS 1)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1006 | (2) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to end on, or to be reckoned to, a particular day, that day shall be included in the period.
@ref s 44(2) (src:1006)
GIVEN edge IS A VicPeriodEdge, anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER edge
    WHEN VicEndsOnDay THEN JUST anchor
    WHEN VicReckonedToDay THEN JUST anchor
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A period of whole days. Counting starts on the day after the anchor (s 44(1)), so the last day is the n-th day after it.
-- src:1005 | (1) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a particular day, that day shall not be included in the period.
@ref s 44(1) (src:1005)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` MEANS anchor PLUS n

-- A period of calendar months. s 44(6)(b) says a month is a calendar month; no section says on which day a period of months ends.
-- Two readings of s 44(1) with s 44(6)(b) are written out, and the answer is given only where they agree.
-- Reading A: the anchor is left out, so counting starts on the next day; the last day is the day before the same-numbered day, n months on from that first day.
-- Reading B: the last day is the day with the anchor's own number, n months on.
-- Each reading is NOTHING where the later month has no day with the number it needs.
-- src:1019 | (b) a reference to a month shall be construed as a reference to a calendar month;
@ref s 44(6)(b) (src:1019)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY firstCounted THEN JUST (target MINUS 1) ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        firstCounted MEANS anchor PLUS 1
        target MEANS Date (DATE_DAY firstCounted) (DATE_MONTH firstCounted PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR firstCounted)

-- src:1019 | (b) a reference to a month shall be construed as a reference to a calendar month;
@ref s 44(6)(b) (src:1019)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY anchor THEN JUST target ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        target MEANS Date (DATE_DAY anchor) (DATE_MONTH anchor PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR anchor)

-- src:1019 | (b) a reference to a month shall be construed as a reference to a calendar month;
@ref s 44(6)(b) (src:1019)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading A` anchor n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day, reading B` anchor n
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST b THEN IF a EQUALS b THEN JUST a ELSE NOTHING

-- s 44(6)(c): a year, without qualification, is a period of twelve months.
-- src:1020 | (c) a reference, without qualification, to a year shall be construed as a reference to a period of twelve months;
@ref s 44(6)(c) (src:1020)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` MEANS
    `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` anchor (n TIMES 12)

-- The one entry point: a period of an amount of a unit, expressed in relation to a day.
-- A week is not defined in the text, so a period of weeks is not covered.
-- src:1005 | (1) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a particular day, that day shall not be included in the period.
@ref s 44(1) (src:1005)
GIVEN edge IS A VicPeriodEdge, amount IS A NUMBER, unit IS A VicPeriodUnit, anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44 last day of a period counted forward from a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER edge
    WHEN VicBeginsOnDay THEN `s44 last day, start left out` unit amount anchor
    WHEN VicReckonedFromDay THEN `s44 last day, start left out` unit amount anchor
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1005 | (1) Where in an Act or subordinate instrument a period of time is expressed to begin on, or to be reckoned from, a particular day, that day shall not be included in the period.
@ref s 44(1) (src:1005)
GIVEN unit IS A VicPeriodUnit, amount IS A NUMBER, anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44 last day, start left out` MEANS
    CONSIDER unit
    WHEN VicDays THEN JUST (`s44(1) last day of a period of n days reckoned from a day` anchor amount)
    WHEN VicWeeks THEN NOTHING
    WHEN VicCalendarMonths THEN `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` anchor amount
    WHEN VicYears THEN `s44(1),(6)(c) last day of n years reckoned from a day` anchor amount

-- s 44(3) and (4): a time limited for the doing of an act or thing that expires or falls on a holiday extends to the next day that is not a holiday.
-- src:1009 | (4) In subsection (3) holiday means—
-- src:1010 | (a) a Saturday or Sunday;
-- src:1012 | (b) a day appointed under the Public Holidays Act 1993 as a public holiday in the place in which the act or thing is to be or may be done.
@ref s 44(4) (src:1009-1012)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, publicHolidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s44(4) a day is a holiday` MEANS
    `is weekend` day OR elem day publicHolidays

-- Looks forward from the given day (inclusive) for a day that is not a holiday; fuel bounds the search.
-- src:1008 | (3) Where the time limited by an Act or subordinate instrument for the doing of any act or thing expires or falls on a day that is a holiday, the time so limited shall extend to, and the act or thing may be done on, the day next following that is not a holiday.
@ref s 44(3) (src:1008)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, fuel IS A NUMBER, publicHolidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF fuel AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        IF `s44(4) a day is a holiday` day publicHolidays THEN `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (day PLUS 1) (fuel MINUS 1) publicHolidays
        OTHERWISE JUST day

-- The day by which the act or thing may be done. It applies to a time limited for doing an act or thing, whatever unit the time was counted in.
-- src:1008 | (3) Where the time limited by an Act or subordinate instrument for the doing of any act or thing expires or falls on a day that is a holiday, the time so limited shall extend to, and the act or thing may be done on, the day next following that is not a holiday.
@ref s 44(3) (src:1008)
GIVEN lastDay IS A DATE, limitedForDoingAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, publicHolidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT limitedForDoingAnAct THEN NOTHING
        IF `s44(4) a day is a holiday` lastDay publicHolidays THEN `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` (lastDay PLUS 1) 400 publicHolidays
        OTHERWISE JUST lastDay

-- A period expressed to be a number of calendar months immediately before a day (s 55(2)(a) words it so).
-- The text says nothing about counting backwards; the same two readings are applied and the answer is given only where they agree.
-- src:1019 | (b) a reference to a month shall be construed as a reference to a calendar month;
@ref s 44(6)(b) (src:1019)
GIVEN beforeDay IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s44(6)(b) first day of n calendar months ending immediately before a day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY readingOne EQUALS DATE_DAY beforeDay AND DATE_DAY readingTwoBase EQUALS DATE_DAY lastDay AND readingOne EQUALS (readingTwoBase PLUS 1)
    THEN JUST readingOne
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS beforeDay MINUS 1
        -- Date does not carry a month below 1 back into the previous year, so the month and year are worked out here.
        sameNumberedDayEarlier d MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (monthIndex d MODULO 12 PLUS 1) (FLOOR (monthIndex d DIVIDED BY 12))
        monthIndex d MEANS DATE_YEAR d TIMES 12 PLUS (DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1) MINUS n
        readingOne MEANS sameNumberedDayEarlier beforeDay
        readingTwoBase MEANS sameNumberedDayEarlier lastDay

§ `Part III -- s 44: the other expressions of time`

-- src:1018 | (a) a reference to midnight, in relation to a particular day, shall be construed as a reference to the point of time at which that day ends;
@ref s 44(6)(a) (src:1018)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s44(6)(a) midnight in relation to a day is the point at which that day ends` MEANS
    VicMoment OF day, VicEndOfDay

-- s 44(6)(d): a financial year is a period of twelve months ending at midnight on 30 June.
-- src:1021 | (d) a reference to a financial year shall be construed as a reference to the period of twelve months ending at midnight on 30 June; and
@ref s 44(6)(d) (src:1021)
GIVEN yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s44(6)(d) midnight at which the financial year ending in a calendar year ends` MEANS
    VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding), VicEndOfDay

-- src:1021 | (d) a reference to a financial year shall be construed as a reference to the period of twelve months ending at midnight on 30 June; and
@ref s 44(6)(d) (src:1021)
GIVEN yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s44(6)(d) first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of a year` MEANS Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1)

-- s 44(6)(e): a calendar year is a period of twelve months ending at midnight on 31 December.
-- src:1022 | (e) a reference to a calendar year shall be construed as a reference to the period of twelve months ending at midnight on 31 December.
@ref s 44(6)(e) (src:1022)
GIVEN yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s44(6)(e) midnight at which a calendar year ends` MEANS
    VicMoment OF (Date 31 12 yearOfEnding), VicEndOfDay

-- src:1022 | (e) a reference to a calendar year shall be construed as a reference to the period of twelve months ending at midnight on 31 December.
@ref s 44(6)(e) (src:1022)
GIVEN yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s44(6)(e) first day of the calendar year ending on 31 December of a year` MEANS Date 1 1 yearOfEnding

-- s 44(7): "now", "heretofore" and "hereafter" refer to the time when the provision came into operation.
-- src:1023 | (7) In a provision of an Act or subordinate instrument the expression "now", "heretofore" or "hereafter" shall be construed as referring to the time when the provision in which the expression occurs came into operation.
@ref s 44(7) (src:1023)
GIVEN provisionCameIntoOperation IS A VicMoment
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s44(7) the time that now, heretofore and hereafter refer to` MEANS provisionCameIntoOperation

-- s 44(5): an expression of time means standard time in Victoria as declared by s 43 of the Supreme Court Act 1986.
-- That section is another Act, not part of the sources; the number of hours standard time runs ahead of Coordinated Universal Time is taken as a given.
-- src:1016 | (5) Subject to section 4 of the Summer Time Act 1972, whenever an expression of time occurs in an Act or subordinate instrument, the time referred to shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be deemed to be standard time throughout Victoria as declared by section 43 of the Supreme Court Act 1986 [endnote 3].
@ref s 44(5) (src:1016)
GIVEN hoursAheadOfUniversalTime IS A NUMBER, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s44(5) hours ahead of Coordinated Universal Time that an expression of time means` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST hoursAheadOfUniversalTime

§ `Part IV -- coming into operation, passing and expiry`

-- s 11(1): a fixed day (in the Act or in a proclamation) starts the Act or provision at the beginning of that day.
-- s 11(2): where the Act gives a power to fix the day by a proclamation published in the Government Gazette, publication is a condition precedent.
-- s 11(2A): a proclamation made on or before the fixed day but published after it takes effect at the beginning of the day it is published.
-- src:110 | (1) Subject to subsection (2) and to section 71 of the Constitution Act 1975, if a particular day is fixed (whether in the Act or in a proclamation made under the Act) for an Act or a provision of an Act to come into operation, the Act or provision comes into operation at the beginning of that day.
-- src:112 | (2) If an Act confers power on the Governor in Council to fix by proclamation published in the Government Gazette a day for the Act or a provision or provisions of the Act to come into operation, the publication of the proclamation in the Government Gazette is a condition precedent to the coming into operation of the Act or provision or provisions in question.
-- src:114 | (2A) If a proclamation fixing a day for the coming into operation of an Act or a provision or provisions of an Act is made on or before the fixed day but is not published in the Government Gazette until after that day, the proclamation does not wholly fail but the Act or provision comes, or the provisions come, into operation at the beginning of the day on which the proclamation is so published.
@ref s 11(1) and s 11(2) and s 11(2A) (src:110-114)
GIVEN fixedDay IS A DATE, powerToProclaim IS A BOOLEAN, publishedOn IS A MAYBE DATE, madeOnOrBeforeFixedDay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicCommencement
`s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT powerToProclaim THEN JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF fixedDay, VicBeginningOfDay))
        IF publishedOn EQUALS NOTHING THEN JUST VicNotYetInOperation
        OTHERWISE `s11 commencement once the proclamation is published` fixedDay publishedOn madeOnOrBeforeFixedDay

-- src:114 | (2A) If a proclamation fixing a day for the coming into operation of an Act or a provision or provisions of an Act is made on or before the fixed day but is not published in the Government Gazette until after that day, the proclamation does not wholly fail but the Act or provision comes, or the provisions come, into operation at the beginning of the day on which the proclamation is so published.
@ref s 11(2A) (src:114)
GIVEN fixedDay IS A DATE, publishedOn IS A MAYBE DATE, madeOnOrBeforeFixedDay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicCommencement
`s11 commencement once the proclamation is published` MEANS
    CONSIDER publishedOn
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST VicNotYetInOperation
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        BRANCH
            IF p AT MOST fixedDay THEN JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF fixedDay, VicBeginningOfDay))
            IF madeOnOrBeforeFixedDay THEN JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF p, VicBeginningOfDay))
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 11(3): the date of the passing of an Act is the date it receives the Royal Assent.
-- src:116 | (3) The date of the passing of an Act is the date on which the Act receives the Royal Assent.
@ref s 11(3) (src:116)
GIVEN royalAssentOn IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s11(3) date of the passing of an Act` MEANS royalAssentOn

-- s 11(4): where the provisions of an Act or portion did not all come into operation on one day, the date of commencement is the first day on or before which all of them have come into operation.
-- src:118 | (4) A reference in an Act to the date of commencement of that Act or another Act or a portion containing 2 or more provisions of that Act or another Act is, if the whole of the Act or portion referred to did not come, or is not to come, into operation on the one day, a reference to the first day on or before which all the provisions of the Act or portion referred to have come, or will have come, into operation.
@ref s 11(4) (src:118)
GIVEN provisionDays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s11(4) date of commencement of an Act or portion whose provisions began on different days` MEANS
    CONSIDER provisionDays
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (foldl `later of` d rest)
    WHERE
        `later of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 10A(3) and (4): where an Act makes no provision for commencement, it is taken to provide for a day to be proclaimed or the first anniversary of the passing, whichever is the earlier.
-- "The first anniversary" is the same-numbered day a year on; the text does not say what it is when that day does not exist.
-- src:104 | (3) If an Act makes no provision for the commencement of a particular provision of the Act, the Act must be taken to provide for the provision to come into operation on a day to be proclaimed or on the first anniversary of the passing of the Act, whichever is the earlier.
@ref s 10A(3) (src:104)
GIVEN passedOn IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY passedOn THEN JUST target ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        target MEANS Date (DATE_DAY passedOn) (DATE_MONTH passedOn) (DATE_YEAR passedOn PLUS 1)

-- src:104 | (3) If an Act makes no provision for the commencement of a particular provision of the Act, the Act must be taken to provide for the provision to come into operation on a day to be proclaimed or on the first anniversary of the passing of the Act, whichever is the earlier.
-- src:106 | (4) If an Act makes no provision for the commencement of the Act or of more than one provision of the Act, the Act must be taken to provide for the Act or those provisions to come into operation on a day or days to be proclaimed or on the first anniversary of the passing of the Act, whichever is the earlier.
@ref s 10A(3) and s 10A(4) (src:104-106)
GIVEN passedOn IS A DATE, proclaimedDay IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s10A(3),(4) day an Act with no commencement provision is taken to come into operation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` passedOn
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST anniversary THEN
        CONSIDER proclaimedDay
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST anniversary
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (IF p AT MOST anniversary THEN p ELSE anniversary)

-- s 12 and s 25: an Act, provision or subordinate instrument expressed to expire, lapse or cease on a day, or to continue in force until a day, continues in operation until the last moment of that day.
-- src:120 | 12 Time of expiry of temporary Acts
-- src:121 | Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to expire, lapse or otherwise cease to have effect on a particular day, or to remain or continue in force until a particular day, the Act or provision shall continue in operation until the last moment of that day.
@ref s 12 (src:120-121)
GIVEN expiryDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s12 moment until which a temporary Act or provision continues in operation` MEANS
    VicMoment OF expiryDay, VicLastMomentOfDay

-- src:278 | 25 Time of expiry of temporary subordinate instruments
-- src:279 | Where a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument is expressed to expire, lapse or otherwise cease to have effect on a particular day, or to remain or continue in force until a particular day, the subordinate instrument or provision shall continue in operation until the last moment of that day.
@ref s 25 (src:278-279)
GIVEN expiryDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A VicMoment
`s25 moment until which a temporary subordinate instrument or provision continues in operation` MEANS
    VicMoment OF expiryDay, VicLastMomentOfDay

-- s 24: a subordinate instrument (not a statutory rule) with a fixed commencement day comes into operation at the beginning of that day.
-- src:275 | 24 Time of commencement of subordinate instruments
-- src:276 | Where in respect of a subordinate instrument (not being a statutory rule) or a provision of such a subordinate instrument a particular day is fixed (whether in the subordinate instrument or in the Act under or pursuant to which the subordinate instrument is made) for it to come into operation, the subordinate instrument or the provision of the subordinate instrument comes into operation at the beginning of that day.
@ref s 24 (src:275-276)
GIVEN fixedDay IS A DATE, isStatutoryRule IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicMoment
`s24 moment a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule comes into operation` MEANS
    IF isStatutoryRule THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (VicMoment OF fixedDay, VicBeginningOfDay)

§ `Part V -- s 49: service by post`

-- s 49(1)(a) and (2)(a): unless the contrary intention appears, service is deemed effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the letter.
-- src:1059 | (a) unless the contrary intention appears, be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter to the person on whom it is to be served; and
-- src:1063 | (a) unless the contrary intention appears, be deemed to be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter either by the registered post or through the certified mail service to the person on whom it is to be served; and
@ref s 49(1)(a) and s 49(2)(a) (src:1059-1063)
GIVEN contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, properlyAddressed IS A BOOLEAN, prepaid IS A BOOLEAN, posted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s49 service by post is deemed effected` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF properlyAddressed AND prepaid AND posted THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 49(1)(b) and (2)(b): unless the contrary is proved, service is deemed effected at the time the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post
-- (or, for registered post and certified mail, would ordinarily be delivered by that service).
-- The day of delivery in the ordinary course is a fact the caller supplies; the text does not say how many days that takes.
-- src:1060 | (b) unless the contrary is proved, be deemed to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
-- src:1064 | (b) unless the contrary is proved, be deemed to have been effected at the time at which the letter would ordinarily be delivered by registered post or through the certified mail service, as the case requires.
@ref s 49(1)(b) and s 49(2)(b) (src:1060-1064)
GIVEN method IS A VicPostMethod, ordinaryDeliveryDay IS A DATE, contraryProved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` MEANS
    CONSIDER method
    WHEN VicOrdinaryPost THEN IF contraryProved THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST ordinaryDeliveryDay
    WHEN VicRegisteredPostOrCertifiedMail THEN IF contraryProved THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST ordinaryDeliveryDay

§ `Part VI -- ages and anniversaries`

-- s 55(2)(b),(c): "had not attained the full age of 18 years before that date". The text does not say on what day an age is attained.
-- The reading taken is the eighteenth anniversary of the birth (the same-numbered day, eighteen years on); a birth on 29 February has no such day in most years, and is not covered.
-- src:1127 | (b) who had not attained the full age of 18 years before that date but whose name could have been so enrolled at any such time if the person had attained that age before that date; or
@ref s 55(2)(b) (src:1127)
GIVEN bornOn IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s55(2) day on which a person born on a day reaches eighteen years, taken as the eighteenth anniversary` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY bornOn THEN JUST target ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        target MEANS Date (DATE_DAY bornOn) (DATE_MONTH bornOn) (DATE_YEAR bornOn PLUS 18)

-- src:1127 | (b) who had not attained the full age of 18 years before that date but whose name could have been so enrolled at any such time if the person had attained that age before that date; or
@ref s 55(2)(b) (src:1127)
GIVEN bornOn IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s55(2)(b) had not attained the full age of 18 years before 26 January 1984` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s55(2) day on which a person born on a day reaches eighteen years, taken as the eighteenth anniversary` bornOn
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST eighteenth THEN JUST (eighteenth AT LEAST `s55(2)(a) day before which the three months are counted`)
